title: Law on Vacant-Homes Uses
new-page: true
choose-if: party_resources > 0 and not parlament_urbanism_passed
subtitle: [? if coming_from_parlament: \[-1 resources\]?]
unavailable-subtitle: [? if parlament_urbanism_passed: Already approved!?][? if not parlament_urbanism_passed and party_resources < 1: Not enough resources.?]
on-arrival: {! 
    if (Q.coming_from_parlament) Q.party_resources -= 1;
    Q.parlament_urbanism_deals = [];
    // TODO: CUP/ERC reaction when part of JxSi // JxCat
!}

= Law on Vacant-Homes Uses

Many large-scale house holding operators, from large banks to a few particulars, hold thousands of homes across Catalonia that sit empty. Be it for speculation, trading, or other reasons, the fact is that this widespread reality is happening in the midst of a huge housing crisis, and many social pressure groups are asking for new actions that attack this practice. The legal strength of such tax-law, however, is blurry as it is unclear where the exact autonomy limits exist in this matter.

- @urbanism_tax: Tax homes kept empty for more than two years
- @urbanism_mobilization: Tax prolonged vacancy and compel large holders to offer the homes

@urbanism_tax
subtitle: A progressive tax on large holders, with exemptions and rebates when homes return to use.
choose-if: player_party != "cup"
unavailable-subtitle: The party rejects such an unambitious proposal for addressing the housing crisis.
on-arrival: parlament_urbanism_variant = "vacancy_tax"
go-to: urbanism_negotiation

Such an unambitious proposal for addressing the housing crisis hardly convinces anyone on the left side of the Parlament. We may want to approach them if we want to secure an ample majority for this vote.


@urbanism_mobilization
subtitle: A steeper tax backed by compulsory rental offers and, as a last resort, Generalitat-approved use orders.
on-arrival: parlament_urbanism_variant = "housing_mobilization"
go-to: urbanism_negotiation

Encroaching this way into private property and the private rental market is not seen kindly by those on the right. We may want to approach them if we want to secure an ample majority for this vote.


@urbanism_negotiation
on-arrival: {!
    var playerProposal = Q.coming_from_parlament;
    var proposingParty = Q.player_in_jxsi ? "jxsi" : Q.player_in_jxcat ? "jxcat" : Q.player_party;
    var targeted = Q.parlament_urbanism_variant == "vacancy_tax";
    var yesNames = targeted
        ? ["ciu","cdc","dl","pdcat","jxsi","jxcat","junts","erc","cs","si"]
        : ["jxsi","erc","cup","psc","icv","csqp","cecp","ecp","si"];
    var noNames = targeted
        ? ["psc","ppc","icv","csqp","cecp","ecp","cup","vox","pxc","fnc"]
        : ["ciu","cdc","dl","pdcat","jxcat","junts","unio","ppc","cs","vox","pxc","fnc"];
    if (playerProposal && !yesNames.includes(proposingParty)) yesNames.push(proposingParty);
    Q.parlament_urbanism_yes_names = yesNames;
    Q.parlament_urbanism_no_names = noNames;

    function canApproach(party, eligible) {
        if (!eligible || !party) return false;
        if ((Q[party + "_parlament_s"] || 0) <= 0) return false;
        if (Q.parlament_urbanism_yes_names.includes(party)) return false;
        return !Q.parlament_urbanism_deals.some(function (deal) { return deal.party == party; });
    }

    var ercPlayer = Q.player_party == "erc";
    var cupPlayer = Q.player_party == "cup";
    Q.parlament_urbanism_can_approach_cup = canApproach("cup", ercPlayer);
    Q.parlament_urbanism_can_approach_psc = canApproach("psc", ercPlayer);
    Q.parlament_urbanism_can_approach_erc = canApproach("erc", cupPlayer);
    Q.parlament_urbanism_can_approach_convergence = canApproach(Q.parlament_current_ciu, ercPlayer || cupPlayer);
    Q.parlament_urbanism_can_approach_icv = canApproach(Q.parlament_current_icv, ercPlayer || cupPlayer);
!}

- @urbanism_approach_cup
- @urbanism_approach_psc
- @urbanism_approach_erc
- @urbanism_approach_convergence
- @urbanism_approach_icv
- @urbanism_vote: Proceed with the vote

@urbanism_approach_cup
title: Approach the CUP before the vote
view-if: parlament_urbanism_can_approach_cup
choose-if: cup_relations > 55
unavailable-subtitle: We don't have good enough relations with the CUP
on-arrival: parlament_urbanism_deal_party = "cup"
go-to: urbanism_make_deal

· The CUP will not oppose our proposal.

@urbanism_approach_psc
title: Approach the PSC before the vote
view-if: parlament_urbanism_can_approach_psc
choose-if: psc_relations > 55
unavailable-subtitle: We don't have good enough relations with the PSC
on-arrival: parlament_urbanism_deal_party = "psc"
go-to: urbanism_make_deal

· The PSC will not oppose our proposal.

@urbanism_approach_erc
title: Approach ERC before the vote
view-if: parlament_urbanism_can_approach_erc
choose-if: erc_relations > 55
unavailable-subtitle: We don't have good enough relations with ERC
on-arrival: parlament_urbanism_deal_party = "erc"
go-to: urbanism_make_deal

· ERC will not oppose our proposal.

@urbanism_approach_convergence
title: Approach [+ parlament_current_ciu +] before the vote
choose-if: (ciu_parlament_s > 0 and ciu_relations > 55) or (cdc_parlament_s > 0 and cdc_relations > 55) or (dl_parlament_s > 0 and dl_relations > 55) or (pdcat_parlament_s > 0 and pdcat_relations > 55) or (jxcat_parlament_s > 0 and jxcat_relations > 55 and not player_in_jxcat) or (junts_parlament_s > 0 and junts_relations > 55)
view-if: parlament_urbanism_can_approach_convergence
unavailable-subtitle: We don't have good enough relations with [+ parlament_current_ciu +]
on-arrival: {!
    Q.parlament_urbanism_deal_party = Q.parlament_current_ciu;
!}
go-to: urbanism_make_deal

· [+ parlament_current_ciu +] will not oppose our proposal.

@urbanism_approach_icv
title: Approach [+ parlament_current_icv +] before the vote
view-if: parlament_urbanism_can_approach_icv
choose-if: (icv_parlament_s > 0 and icv_relations > 55) or (csqp_parlament_s > 0 and csqp_relations > 55) or (cecp_parlament_s > 0 and cecp_relations > 55) or (ecp_parlament_s > 0 and ecp_relations > 55)
unavailable-subtitle: We don't have good enough relations with [+ parlament_current_icv +]
on-arrival: {!
    Q.parlament_urbanism_deal_party = Q.parlament_current_icv;
!}
go-to: urbanism_make_deal

· [+ parlament_current_icv +] will not oppose our proposal.

@urbanism_make_deal
on-arrival: {!
    var party = Q.parlament_urbanism_deal_party;
    var baselineNo = Q.parlament_urbanism_no_names.includes(party);
    var newPosition = baselineNo && Q[party + "_relations"] <= 65 ? "abstain" : "yes";
    Q.parlament_urbanism_deals.push({party: party, position: newPosition});
    Q[party + "_relations"] -= 5;
!}
go-to: urbanism_negotiation

@urbanism_vote
subtitle: [? if not parlament_urbanism_deal_party: Who needs their support anyway? ?]
on-arrival: {!
    var playerProposal = Q.coming_from_parlament;
    var proposingParty = Q.player_in_jxsi ? "jxsi" : Q.player_in_jxcat ? "jxcat" : Q.player_party;
    Q.coming_from_parlament = false;

    var author = Q.player_in_jxsi ? "jxsi" : Q.player_in_jxcat ? "jxcat" : Q.player_party;
    var donor = Q.parlament_current_icv;
    var proposalYoung = Q.parlament_urbanism_variant == "vacancy_tax" ? 0.075 : 0.165;
    var proposalUnemployed = Q.parlament_urbanism_variant == "vacancy_tax" ? 0.105 : 0.225;
    var proposalMiddle = Q.parlament_urbanism_variant == "vacancy_tax" ? 0.045 : 0.09;
    for (const c of Q.parlament_constituencies) {
        Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_young_support"] += proposalYoung;
        Q[donor + "_parlament_" + c + "_young_support"] -= proposalYoung;
        Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_unemployed_support"] += proposalUnemployed;
        Q[donor + "_parlament_" + c + "_unemployed_support"] -= proposalUnemployed;
        Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_middle_support"] += proposalMiddle;
        Q[donor + "_parlament_" + c + "_middle_support"] -= proposalMiddle;
    }

    var targeted = Q.parlament_urbanism_variant == "vacancy_tax";
    var yesNames = targeted
        ? ["ciu","cdc","dl","pdcat","jxsi","jxcat","junts","erc","cs","si"]
        : ["jxsi","erc","cup","psc","icv","csqp","cecp","ecp","si"];
    var noNames = targeted
        ? ["psc","ppc","icv","csqp","cecp","ecp","cup","vox","pxc","fnc"]
        : ["ciu","cdc","dl","pdcat","jxcat","junts","unio","ppc","cs","vox","pxc","fnc"];
    if (playerProposal && !yesNames.includes(proposingParty)) yesNames.push(proposingParty);
    for (const deal of (Q.parlament_urbanism_deals || [])) {
        yesNames = yesNames.filter(function (party) { return party != deal.party; });
        noNames = noNames.filter(function (party) { return party != deal.party; });
        if (deal.position == "yes") yesNames.push(deal.party);
    }
    var all = ["ciu","cdc","dl","pdcat","jxsi","jxcat","junts","erc","cup","psc","ppc","cs","icv","csqp","cecp","ecp","unio","si","vox","pxc","fnc"];
    var labels = {ciu:"CiU",cdc:"CDC",dl:"DL",pdcat:"PDeCAT",jxsi:"JxSí",jxcat:"JxCat",junts:"Junts",erc:"ERC",cup:"CUP",psc:"PSC",ppc:"PPC",cs:"Cs",icv:"ICV-EUiA",csqp:"CSQP",cecp:"CECP",ecp:"ECP",unio:"UDC",si:"SI",vox:"Vox",pxc:"PxC",fnc:"FNC"};
    var yesParties = [], noParties = [], abstainParties = [];
    Q.parlament_urbanism_yes = 0;
    Q.parlament_urbanism_no = 0;
    Q.parlament_urbanism_abst = 0;
    for (const p of all) {
        var seats = Q[p + "_parlament_s"] || 0;
        if (seats <= 0) continue;
        if (yesNames.includes(p)) {
            Q.parlament_urbanism_yes += seats;
            yesParties.push({label: labels[p]});
        } else if (noNames.includes(p)) {
            Q.parlament_urbanism_no += seats;
            noParties.push({label: labels[p]});
        } else {
            Q.parlament_urbanism_abst += seats;
            abstainParties.push({label: labels[p]});
        }
    }
    Q.parlament_urbanism_passed = Q.parlament_urbanism_yes > Q.parlament_urbanism_no;
    Q.parlament_urbanism_vote_result = {outcomes:[
        {kind:"yes",label:"Yes",votes:Q.parlament_urbanism_yes,parties:yesParties},
        {kind:"abstain",label:"Abstention",votes:Q.parlament_urbanism_abst,parties:abstainParties},
        {kind:"no",label:"No",votes:Q.parlament_urbanism_no,parties:noParties}
    ]};

    if (Q.parlament_urbanism_passed) {
        var passageYoung = targeted ? 0.175 : 0.385;
        var passageUnemployed = targeted ? 0.245 : 0.525;
        var passageMiddle = targeted ? 0.105 : 0.21;
        for (const c of Q.parlament_constituencies) {
            Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_young_support"] += passageYoung;
            Q[donor + "_parlament_" + c + "_young_support"] -= passageYoung;
            Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_unemployed_support"] += passageUnemployed;
            Q[donor + "_parlament_" + c + "_unemployed_support"] -= passageUnemployed;
            Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_middle_support"] += passageMiddle;
            Q[donor + "_parlament_" + c + "_middle_support"] -= passageMiddle;
        }
        if (targeted) {
            G.registerLaw(Q, {id:"vacant_homes_tax",title:"Vacant Homes Tax",icon:"img/community_icon.svg",targets:{generalitat_surplus:0.025,welfare_index_growth:0.05,social_dissent_eq:-1},ramp_ticks:12});
        } else {
            G.registerLaw(Q, {id:"vacant_homes_mobilization",title:"Vacant Homes Mobilization",icon:"img/community_icon.svg",targets:{generalitat_surplus:0.015,welfare_index_growth:0.12,unemployment_recovery:0.02,gdp_growth:-0.04,social_dissent_eq:-2},ramp_ticks:6});
        }
        Q.constitutional_vacant_homes_countdown = 30;
        Q.countdowns.push("constitutional_vacant_homes");
    }
!}

<div data-widget="chamber-vote" data-props='{"configFrom":"parlament_urbanism_vote_result"}'></div>

[? if parlament_urbanism_passed: The Parlament has approved the bill! While social housing pressure groups are[? if parlament_urbanism_variant = "vacancy_tax": cautiously ?] celebrating along with our party's lawmakers, [? if parlament_urbanism_variant = "vacancy_tax": the left of the Parlament is criticizing the law for its lack of ambition and, of course, we also?] the usual PP-filed legal challenge for it is already in motion. We'll have to see how it evolves... ?]
[? if not parlament_urbanism_passed: The Parlament has rejected the bill, to the dismay of many of our representatives and many in the social housing pressure groups back on the streets. ?]

- @post_event: Continue...
